    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1033">

                <pb facs="1088" n="1078" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1078"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93 Tibet/7–849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-08T18:00:00+08:00">July 8, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:26 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1459. We like suggestion Embassy, New Delhi, to send small mission this summer to
                    Lhasa (Department’s intel July 5, 1 a. m.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d1033-f1"/>).
                    Authority Canton Government over Tibet non-existent and we agree any move with
                    implications recognition autonomous status Tibet should be made before relations
                    established with Chinese Communist government.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1459, repeated New Delhi 6.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
